the actual destination.

00:05:41.849 --> 00:05:43.361
So as long as you are moving,

00:05:43.361 --> 00:05:45.118
as long as you are working,

00:05:45.118 --> 00:05:46.803
that is the destination.

00:05:46.803 --> 00:05:49.078
- Wow.
- Yeah, the journey.

00:05:49.078 --> 00:05:50.217
- But really it is simply that

00:05:50.217 --> 00:05:51.769
the journey is the destination.

00:05:51.769 --> 00:05:52.828
- [Woman] I agree.

00:05:52.828 --> 00:05:54.606
As long as you're working you're good.

00:05:54.606 --> 00:05:56.950
As a writer you start
trying different things

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.927
and you try different chords

00:05:58.927 --> 00:06:00.754
or different structures of songs.

00:06:00.754 --> 00:06:02.653
Different beats that you've never really

00:06:02.653 --> 00:06:05.602
explored that path before.

00:06:05.602 --> 00:06:06.851
You know ...

00:06:06.851 --> 00:06:11.299
And I think having always
been a writer first,

00:06:11.299 --> 00:06:13.615
I'm obsessed with the syncopation of

00:06:13.615 --> 00:06:17.290
the way that words sound when
they're said a certain way

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.810
and once I've kind of done something once,

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.752
I always want to go to
a different direction

00:06:21.752 --> 00:06:23.309
and never repeat myself.

00:06:23.309 --> 00:06:27.142
So as a writer, I think
that I've always hoped

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:29.902
that my music would
constantly be changing.

00:06:29.902 --> 00:06:34.305
Because you never want to
make the same album twice,

00:06:34.305 --> 00:06:35.994
the same song twice.

00:06:35.994 --> 00:06:37.077
And you know,

00:06:38.135 --> 00:06:41.736
my greatest hope has been that as I grow

00:06:41.736 --> 00:06:43.235
my fans will grow up with me

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:45.553
and as I change and my life changes,

00:06:45.553 --> 00:06:47.281
my music will change as well.

00:06:47.281 --> 00:06:49.222
